{"id":"word:hebrew:H8552","type":"word","title":"תָּמַם","subtitle":"H8552 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to complete , in a good or a bad sense, literal, or figurative, transitive or intransitive","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to תָּמַם (H8552) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 63 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"תָּמַם (tâmam) means to complete , in a good or a bad sense, literal, or figurative, transitive or intransitive First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 6 22."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"תָּמַם","transliteration":"tâmam","pronunciation":"taw-mam'","strong":"H8552","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8552","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["תֹּ֥ם","תֻּמָּֽ/ם","תַּ֥מּוּ","תֹּם֙","תֹּ֣ם"],"morphs":[["HVqc",10],["HVqp3cp",10],["HVqc/Sp3mp",6],["HVqi3mp",5],["HVqp3ms",4],["HVqp1cp",4],["HC/Vqw3fs",2],["HVti2ms",2],["HC/Vqq3cp",2],["HVqc/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to complete , in a good or a bad sense, literal, or figurative, transitive or intransitive","usage":"accomplish, cease, be clean (pass-) ed, consume, have done, (come to an, have an, make an) end, fail, come to the full, be all gone, × be all here, be (make) perfect, be spent, sum, be (shew self) upright, be wasted, whole.","full":"H8552. tamam [ תָּמַם ], תַּם verb be complete, finished (Arabic id. , Phoenician תם , Syriac derived species and derivatives; compare Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew (rare), Aramaic תְּמִימָא , perfect ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular תַּם Gen 47:18 3 t. (+ Qr תַּם מֵאֵשׁ֯ Jer 6:29 ); 3plural תַּמּוּ Deut 2:16 +; תָּ֑מּוּ 2Kin 7:13 ; 1 plural תַּמְנוּ (Ges § 67dd ) Numbers 17:28; Psa 64:7 ; תָּ֑מְנוּ Jer 44:18 ; ( Lam 3:22 read ᵑ6 ᵑ7 תַּמּוּ Ew Löhr Bu); Imperfect 3masculine singular יִתֹּם (Ges § 67g ) Gen 47:15 ; Ezek 47:12 ; 3 feminine singular תִתֻּם 24:11 (Ges § 67q ; strike out Co), תִּתֹּם Gen 47:18 ; 1Kin 7:22 ; 1 singular אֵיתָ֑ם Psa 19:14 ; 3 masculine plural יִתַּ֫מּוּ Num 14:35 +, וַיִּתְּמוּ Deut 34:8 ; Infinitive construct תֹּם Lev 25:29 10 t.; תָּםֿ Isa 18:5 ; suffix תֻּתִּי Jer 27:8 7 t. suffix; — 1 be finished, completed ; the writing of words Deut 31:24 , 30 (see Dr.; J), Job 31:40 ; building of temple 1Kin 6:22 , compare 7:22 ; fulfilled , ׳י 's command (by obedience) Josh 4:10 (E); as auxil. + finite verb = completely, wholly, entirely , נִבְתָ֑וּ תַּמּוּ 3:16 (E) were wholly cut off ; תַמּוּ סָפוּ Psa 73:19 entirely consumed ; followed by ל infinitive: לעבור תַּמּוּ were finished in regard to , etc., i.e. were entirely passed over Josh 3:17 ; 4:1 , 11 (JE) 2Sam 15:24 ; לחמּול Josh 5:8 (E) entirely circumcised , Numbers 17:28. 2 be finished, come to an end, cease: the year, Gen 47:18 (J), Lev 25:29 (P), Jer 1:3 ; the years of ׳י have no end Psa 102:28 ; days of weeping Deut 34:8 (P), compare Lam 4:22 ; also Isa 18:5 ; Lam 3:22 . 3 be complete , of number, 1Sam 16:11 . 4 be consumed, exhausted, spent: silver Gen 47:15 , 18 (J); strength Lev 26:20 (H); lead Jer 6:29 (Qr); bread 37:21 ; fruit Ezek 47:12 ; rust 24:11 . 5 be finished, consumed, destroyed: people Num 14:33 (J), 14:35 ; Numbers 17:28 (P; || מות ). 32:13 (J), Josh 8:24 ; 10:20 (JE), Deut 2:14-15 , 16 ; Josh 5:6 (D), 1Kin 14:10 ; 2Kin 7:13 ; Isa 16:4 ; Jer 14:15 ; 24:10 ; 27:8 ; 36:23 ; 44:12 (twice in verse); 44:18 , 27 ; Psa 9:7 (but read דַּמּוּ ), 104:35 . 6 be complete, sound, unimpaired , ethically, Psa 19:14 (|| נִקָּה ; late). 7 twice, very strangely, si vera 1., transitive: Psa 64:7 תמנו we have completed (read probably הֲתִמֹּנוּ ); Jer 27:8 בְּיָדוֺ אֹתָם עַדתֻּֿמֹּי (read with Gr תִּתִּי ). Hiph`il Perfect 1singular הֲתִמֹּ֫תִי Ezek 22:15 ; 3 masculine plural הֵחַמּ֫וּ 2Sam 20:18 ; Imperfect יַתֵּם 2Kin 22:4 ; 2 masculine singular תַּתֵּם Job 22:3 (Ges § 67y ); Infinitive absolute הָחֵם Ezek 24:10 ; construct, id. , Dan 8:23 + 9:24 Qr (see Dr.); suffix הֲִתמְךְ (Ges § 67v ) Isa 33:1 ; &#8212; 1 finish, complete, perfect , a matter 2Sam 20:18 (but Qal , come to an end , with ה interrogative, We Dr and others); flesh in cooking Ezek 24:10 . 2 finish, cease doing a thing, followed by participle (Ges § 120b ), שׁוֺדֵד Isa 33:1 . 3 complete, sum up , with accusative money 2Kin 22:4 (other conjectures Klo Gr Gi); transgressions Dan 8:23 ; sin 9:24 (Qr; Kt חתם ). 4 destroy uncleanness, with מן from , Ezek 22:15 . 5 causative (of Qal 6 ): accusative דרכיך Job 22:3 make sound thy ways. Hithpa`el Imperfect 2masculine singular תִּתַּמָּם 2Sam 22:26 , with עִם deal in integrity with = Psa 18:26 (late, see Qal 6 ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 6 22","keyReferences":["1Kgs 6 22","1Kgs 7 22","1Kgs 14 10","1Sam 16 11","2Kgs 7 13","2Kgs 22 4","2Sam 15 24","2Sam 20 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":63,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 6 22","book":"1Kgs","chapter":6,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תֹּ֣ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 7 22","book":"1Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תִּתֹּ֖ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3fs"},{"reference":"1Kgs 14 10","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תֻּמּֽ/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 16 11","book":"1Sam","chapter":16,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֲ/תַ֣מּוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTi/Vqp3cp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 7 13","book":"2Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תָּ֑מּוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3cp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 22 4","book":"2Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יַתֵּ֣ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhi3ms"},{"reference":"2Sam 15 24","book":"2Sam","chapter":15,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תֹּ֥ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqc"},{"reference":"2Sam 20 18","book":"2